{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "return_aware_cluster_bonus",
  "intent": "Extends the parent's return-aware regret heuristic by adding a bounded cluster_density bonus (0.1 * cluster_density). Candidates in dense neighborhoods—those with a high fraction of other unvisited nodes within mean distance—receive a small priority boost that reinforces contiguous cluster traversal in clustered instances and slightly biases toward marginally denser local structure in uniform instances. The bonus complements the parent's nonlinear regret term: while r/(0.5+nr) already amplifies regret when the nearest alternative is close, cluster_density directly rewards nodes surrounded by many close neighbors, helping distinguish cluster-interior from cluster-boundary candidates. The contribution is bounded (≤0.1) so the local distance term remains dominant, matching the TSP heuristic g",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    denom = 0.5 + nr\n    if denom < 1e-9:\n        denom = 1e-9\n    return -d + 0.25 * rd + 0.2 * r + 0.15 * r / denom + 0.1 * cd",
  "source": "live_llm",
